# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Trustfile — Trust boundaries and integrity invariants for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# What LLM/SLM agents are trusted to do without asking, and integrity
# invariants that verify the repo has not been tampered with.

@abstract:
Trust boundaries and integrity checks for progblocks. A small, dependency-
free browser component with no server component and no runtime
dependencies — but its whole job is rendering untrusted documentation
content. Until 2026-10-05 it had a real, unescaped-innerHTML injection
surface; that was closed by rendering all author and reader text through
textContent (see ../descriptiles/NEUROSYM.a2ml,
../contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml). The trust model below keeps it closed.
@end

## Trust Level

Current trust level: standard

- Agent may read and edit the component source, tests, and machine-readable
  metadata freely.
- Agent must NOT widen trust of variant content or variable values (for
  example rendering them as markup, or adding a sanitiser allowlist)
  without flagging it — rendering and sanitisation choices here are
  security-sensitive and reviewed, not silently patched in.
- Never re-inline action SHAs that .github/workflows/actions.lock owns.
- Never hand-edit progblocks-launcher.sh — it is generated.
- Licence, org, and CLADE identity fields are maintainer-only.

## Integrity Invariants

### no-secrets-committed
- description: No credential files in repo
- run: test ! -f .env && test ! -f credentials.json
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: .github/workflows/secret-scanner.yml (gitleaks)

### no-private-keys
- description: No private key files committed
- run: "! find . -not -path './node_modules/*' -not -path './.git/*' \( -name '*.pem' -o -name '*.key' -o -name 'id_rsa' -o -name 'id_ed25519' \) 2>/dev/null | head -1 | grep -q ."
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: .github/workflows/secret-scanner.yml (gitleaks)

### no-tokens-in-source
- description: No hardcoded API tokens in the component source
- run: "! grep -rniE '(api[_-]?key|secret|token|password)[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*.?[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}' src/ 2>/dev/null | grep -q ."
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: .github/workflows/secret-scanner.yml (gitleaks)

## Provenance

### author-correct
- description: Git author matches expected identity
- run: "git log -1 --format='%ae' | grep -qE '(hyperpolymath|j\\.d\\.a\\.jewell)'"
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### license-content
- description: LICENSE is the canonical MPL-2.0 text
- run: grep -q 'Mozilla Public License Version 2.0' LICENSE
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

## Sensitive areas requiring explicit approval

- GOVERNANCE.md
- .github/CODEOWNERS
- LICENSE
- .github/workflows/actions.lock (the pin — do not re-inline SHAs)
- progblocks-launcher.sh (generated — never hand-edit; fix progblocks.launcher.a2ml's source or the upstream launch-scaffolder instead)
- .machine_readable/descriptiles/CLADE.a2ml (repo identity — never copy another repo's UUID/name)
- src/prog-block.js's rendering path (el(), _readLightDom(), _renderVariant(), _renderValues()) — must stay textContent-only; it replaced the former innerHTML XSS surface
